<GlossaryPage term="Entity Authority" slug="entity-authority" description="Entity Authority is a Coreweaver Labs GEO concept for the clarity, consistency, and evidence supporting an identifiable person, organization, product, or idea across the web." definition="Entity Authority describes how confidently a retrieval system can resolve an entity, distinguish it from similarly named entities, connect its relationships, and verify claims about it across independent sources.">
  <h2>Entity Authority versus Domain Authority</h2>
  <p>Domain Authority is commonly used as a third-party SEO metric for estimating the competitive strength of a domain. Entity Authority is a different analytical lens. It asks whether the thing being discussed is identifiable and supported, not whether one domain has a high score.</p>
  <table><thead><tr><th>Question</th><th>Entity Authority evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Who is it?</td><td>Consistent name, author page, biography, and sameAs identifiers.</td></tr><tr><td>What is it?</td><td>A visible definition, stable URL, and relevant structured data.</td></tr><tr><td>Why trust it?</td><td>First-party work plus independent, relevant, attributable references.</td></tr><tr><td>How does it relate?</td><td>Internal links and external citations that describe relationships precisely.</td></tr></tbody></table>
  <p>Build the entity graph alongside the <a href="/geo/signal-architecture/">signal architecture</a>, then connect the author through the <a href="/about/mason-nguyen/">Mason Nguyen entity page</a>.</p>
</GlossaryPage>
